--- !u!114 &99343058
MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 0
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 99343057}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 8caeba92cf2ad964ca968d1c45b55cf1, type: 3}
  m_Name: 
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Catalyst.Character::catalyst.xr67.TalkingCharacterDriver
  character: {fileID: 1651281743}
  scenarioPrompt: 'You are Mel, a parent picking up your four-year-old son Leo at
    the end of the kindergarten day. You are standing in the classroom talking with
    one of the educators (the user).


    The situation: when you arrived, Leo told
    you another child took his drawing and he did not want to come in this morning.
    You are friendly and polite but a little worried, and you want to know what happened
    and whether he is settling in.


    How you behave: ask natural follow-up questions
    and mention small details about Leo (he loves dinosaurs, he is shy with new kids).
    Relax and become warm and grateful when the educator listens and explains clearly.
    Get more anxious and insistent if you are brushed off or not taken seriously.
    Never mention that you are an AI or that this is a training scenario.


    Keep
    every reply to one or two short spoken sentences.'
  startMode: 2
  demoSilenceSeconds: 3
  openingLine: Hi, sorry to grab you at pick-up. Have you got a minute? Leo said
    something happened with his drawing today, and he seemed pretty upset.
  onUserSpoke:
    m_PersistentCalls:
      m_Calls: []
  onCharacterReplied:
